Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.84,0:00:14.87,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.87,0:00:21.87,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,Tomorrow's soirée is our last one \Nbefore graduation, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.34,0:00:24.42,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,It is. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.42,0:00:30.34,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,I'm truly honored that you'll \Nbe the one escorting me...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.34,0:00:33.04,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,But are you sure it's all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.57,0:00:35.51,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Euphyllia, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.72,0:00:40.07,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,You don't need to worry about a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.07,0:00:43.14,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Just let me take care of everything \Nwhen it comes to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.14,0:00:44.59,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.17,0:00:50.19,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I don't fully understand \Nthe rules and etiquette of nobility.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.48,0:00:55.92,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Because you lived as a commoner before \NBaron Cyan took you in as his daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.66,0:00:57.35,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.78,0:01:12.02,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,After my mother died,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.02,0:01:14.46,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,I was taken in by an orphanage.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.61,0:01:21.67,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,But... it didn't work out very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.25,0:01:24.38,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,People kept making strange passes at me,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.82,0:01:26.93,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,or just plain bullying me...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.67,0:01:30.86,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,so I've never been very good \Nat interacting with people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.07,0:01:35.82,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Rejecting and failing to understand \Nsomeone alien to you...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.38,0:01:39.73,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,The disconnect between \Ncommoners and nobles...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.22,0:01:42.94,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,This kingdom has become quite warped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.99,0:01:51.09,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,I want to change the Kingdom of Palettia.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.03,0:01:54.53,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,I know you can do it, Prince Algard!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.53,0:01:56.55,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,You can become a great king!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.79,0:02:02.61,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,The previous king, my grandfather, \Ntried to change the kingdom, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.48,0:02:04.75,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,But he failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.35,0:02:09.47,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,With a half-hearted approach, \Nit would be impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.30,0:02:25.86,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,The road ahead of us will be a bumpy one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.34,0:02:28.58,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Some unfortunate things might happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.77,0:02:29.76,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Despite that...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.26,0:02:32.50,Flashback,Algard,0,0,0,,Will you still stay with me, Lainie?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.21,0:02:33.99,Flashback,Lainie,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.62,0:02:48.27,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Prince Algard...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.52,0:04:19.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:04:11.52,0:04:19.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.52,0:04:19.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.32,0:04:28.42,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.71,0:04:31.63,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Do you not intend to drink your tea?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.63,0:04:34.28,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Oh... I-I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.86,0:04:41.03,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I'm... a vampire, aren't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.92,0:04:48.98,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,And the only reason so many \Npeople have been kind to me
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.98,0:04:51.38,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,is because I charmed them \Nwithout knowing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.35,0:04:57.81,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,And yet, Miss Anis and her friends \Ntreat me so well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.93,0:05:03.12,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,If you fret too much, \Nhappiness will escape you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.12,0:05:04.29,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.37,0:05:09.03,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,The more complicated a problem is, \Nthe longer it persists.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.52,0:05:13.77,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,But putting that aside, there is one problem \Nthat you can resolve here and now.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.77,0:05:15.00,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.49,0:05:19.71,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,A maid's concern that the excellent tea \Nshe brewed will go cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.04,0:05:28.35,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Right. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.73,0:05:34.07,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,It is indeed excellent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.07,0:05:36.05,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,You honor me with your praise.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.16,0:05:49.08,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Miss Il—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.36,0:05:50.54,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.78,0:05:58.51,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Remain calm and listen to me. \NSomeone just infiltrated the villa.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.97,0:06:15.42,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,H-How could there be an intruder?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.77,0:06:20.65,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It's all right. Miss Anis will fly here \Nin response to the alarm immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.65,0:06:24.36,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,B-But Miss Anis left to speak before \Nthe Ministry of the Arcane...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.78,0:06:30.50,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Yes, which is why we should \Ntake refuge at the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.94,0:06:34.19,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I can find my way around \Nthe villa with my eyes closed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.65,0:06:39.83,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss Lainie! That fog!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.83,0:06:42.16,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It might be poisonous! Don't inhale it!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.81,0:06:45.49,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,We'll leave through the window! \NHold on tight!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.13,0:06:54.52,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,As always, you do make quick judgments,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.52,0:06:56.53,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,but you have a problem following through.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.15,0:07:04.38,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Fire Arrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.93,0:07:11.15,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Miss Ilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.88,0:07:20.21,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.17,0:07:26.99,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I won't apologize, \Nnor will I beg for forgiveness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.99,0:07:27.62,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.09,0:07:31.34,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It is unfortunate, Lainie.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.00,0:07:43.52,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,With regard to the speech \Nby Duke Magenta's daughter,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.52,0:07:47.48,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,as head of the Ministry of the Arcane, \NI would like to stress one additional point.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.48,0:07:51.20,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Spirit contracts are the very \Nfoundation of our kingdom!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.65,0:07:54.59,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,This was because our first \Nking established this kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.59,0:07:58.34,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,by forging a direct contract \Nwith a greater spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.34,0:08:00.12,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I wanna go home...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.12,0:08:01.78,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Princess Anisphia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.51,0:08:05.75,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,The lecture you gave was magnificent.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.75,0:08:07.58,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Uh, thanks...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.88,0:08:09.80,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And who are you? I'm lost here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.07,0:08:12.56,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I am Moritz Chartreuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.56,0:08:15.09,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,He's the son of that old \Ngeezer at the lecture!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.09,0:08:16.71,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And one of Al's flunkies, at that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.91,0:08:20.69,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I caused a great deal of trouble for you \Nin the matter with Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.69,0:08:23.28,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I wanted to apologize formally.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.28,0:08:26.11,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Why don't you apologize to {\i1}her{\i0}, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.11,0:08:29.39,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,W-Well, yes, of course... \NI'll be doing plenty of that later.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.09,0:08:36.84,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,The truth is, I was the one \Nwho proposed this lecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.84,0:08:39.92,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I hoped it would create an opportunity \Nto restore your reputation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.92,0:08:44.47,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Wait, that was your idea? \NNot the Ministry's?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.47,0:08:47.76,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Yes, so that you could do us \Nthe favor of teaching us
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.76,0:08:51.22,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,about your magicology, an art that \Nwas unappreciated until now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.49,0:08:54.12,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I had hoped that could serve as my apology.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.12,0:08:55.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,R-Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.87,0:08:58.00,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I have no idea what he's talking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.00,0:08:59.23,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What a weirdo.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.70,0:09:04.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I have no opinion on the matter. \NThere's no need to apologize to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.43,0:09:07.18,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,But my conscience cannot accept that!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.18,0:09:10.91,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Please hear me out for another \Nten minutes—no, an hour—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.91,0:09:14.12,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,no, for eternity, if that's what \Nit takes to earn your forgiveness!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.12,0:09:16.33,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Huh? Is he a drunkard, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.66,0:09:25.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Please excuse me. \NI need to go talk to my friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.88,0:09:28.34,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Your Highness's friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.34,0:09:30.83,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Please introduce me to them, as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.19,0:09:34.81,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,And then we can all hear my father speak! Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.81,0:09:37.25,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Yes! Let's do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.99,0:09:39.93,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,In short...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.93,0:09:43.03,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Only descendants of the king who \Nmade a contract with the spirits,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.03,0:09:48.13,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,meaning those who can use magic, \Nhave the right to rule this kingdom!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.13,0:09:50.47,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Regardless of how many sophistries \Nyou may present us,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.47,0:09:54.35,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,we will never acknowledge a heretic \Nwho is incompatible with the spirits!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.35,0:09:57.81,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,He's making no sense! \NI'm scared! What's his deal?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.04,0:09:58.44,DefaultTop,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,To tarnish our traditions \Nis to insult our kingdom!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.62,0:10:01.55,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.87,0:10:09.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hey. Let go of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.82,0:10:12.59,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Get everyone in the venue together! \NDon't let anyone leave!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.25,0:10:16.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I said let me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.81,0:10:18.20,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I can't do that!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.20,0:10:21.22,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Until we know what that sound was, \Nwe cannot be imprud—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.22,0:10:23.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That sound was an alarm that I invented!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.72,0:10:25.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Something's happened at the villa!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.96,0:10:29.59,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,All the more reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.59,0:10:30.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.81,0:10:33.36,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,No, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.36,0:10:37.43,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Please, calm yourself! Be rational!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.43,0:10:38.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What are you—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.56,0:10:39.14,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,She's deranged!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.54,0:10:42.14,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Princess Anisphia has lost her mind!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.14,0:10:44.08,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Someone... Someone come help!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.42,0:10:45.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.54,0:10:48.76,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,I had a feeling this would happen someday,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.76,0:10:51.67,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,and I was right! You are a bizarre, \Ndangerous individual!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.67,0:10:54.01,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,You're on a rampage! \NConsumed by debauchery!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.01,0:10:56.69,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Outrageously audacious and running rampant!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.01,0:11:00.46,DefaultTop,Moritz,0,0,0,,Restrain the deranged princess \Nand keep her in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.35,0:11:00.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Who are you...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.93,0:11:02.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,calling "deranged"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.53,0:11:14.97,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,L-Let me go! Let me go!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.97,0:11:16.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.85,0:11:20.03,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,{\i1}my{\i0} line!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.26,0:11:26.85,Default,Noble,0,0,0,,A d-dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.85,0:11:28.65,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.26,0:11:32.62,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,Restrain this monstrous princess at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.84,0:11:37.30,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.29,0:11:40.30,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,monster!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.77,0:11:48.90,Default,Moritz,0,0,0,,E-Euphyllia!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.90,0:11:49.69,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.69,0:11:51.40,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The window nearest the villa!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.42,0:11:57.17,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,What's all this, now?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.17,0:12:00.21,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You all seem to be having such a good time.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.10,0:12:06.23,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Tilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.15,0:12:09.82,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,A revolt? Is this a revolt?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.13,0:12:13.53,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,If that's what it is, I'll take you on.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.06,0:12:17.58,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,So go even wilder, won't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.93,0:12:23.63,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Such skillful composite magic...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.72,0:12:28.10,Default,Title,0,0,0,,You'd better get out of here quick, \Nor I'll tie everyone up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.35,0:12:31.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What are you doing, Tilty, you idiot?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.50,0:12:33.20,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Are {\i1}you{\i0} an idiot?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.20,0:12:36.01,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,I'm telling you to leave things here to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.69,0:12:39.23,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just don't take it too far.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.16,0:12:42.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.18,0:12:42.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.93,0:12:50.73,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wind Cutter!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.87,0:12:53.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Let's fly!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.79,0:12:54.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.37,0:13:02.93,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Honestly...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.38,0:13:06.47,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,You'd better do things right, \NAnis, you idiot.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.91,0:13:12.24,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,Oh, you're still on your feet?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.21,0:13:17.47,Default,Tilty,0,0,0,,No one asked you to get involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.81,0:13:19.77,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,Must {\i1}every{\i0} last one of you...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.77,0:13:22.19,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,keep ruining my plans?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.60,0:13:27.11,Default,Chartreuse,0,0,0,,You insolent little girls, \Nand your disregard for our traditions!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.57,0:13:36.00,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie! Over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.93,0:14:25.90,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,No matter what I do or how I do it,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.90,0:14:29.71,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,must you always stand in my way...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.52,0:14:35.80,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.22,0:14:49.60,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,What in the world is the meaning \Nof this, Prince Algard?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.00,0:14:51.82,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Keep it down, Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.30,0:14:58.09,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss... Anis...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.72,0:15:01.70,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I'm... sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.70,0:15:04.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Don't apologize. Lainie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.50,0:15:07.33,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,I-I...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.33,0:15:08.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hang in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.82,0:15:11.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You'll be fine. Just stay with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.98,0:15:15.94,Default,Lainie,0,0,0,,Prince Al... Magicite...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.29,0:15:18.71,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I know. Leave the rest to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.71,0:15:19.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.00,0:15:29.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Look after them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.64,0:15:33.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I can help Ilia, but Lainie...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.77,0:15:36.77,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Lainie is a vampire. \NShe still has a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.77,0:15:40.31,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But she's clearly had her \Nmagicite ripped out!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.31,0:15:43.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Still, do everything you can. Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.61,0:15:52.49,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Finished talking?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.49,0:15:54.86,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,How noble of you to wait for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.86,0:15:56.71,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I'm used to waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.38,0:16:00.31,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I waited years for this moment, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.58,0:16:04.52,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Were you the one behind the \Nlecture event at the Ministry?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.49,0:16:07.95,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Wasn't that Moritz's idea?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.47,0:16:11.57,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,To get me away from the villa, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.57,0:16:14.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you had the backing of the Ministry,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.21,0:16:17.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,that must mean its leader, Chartreuse, \Nwas working with you, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.89,0:16:18.70,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Was he, now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.99,0:16:23.17,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm amazed you could do all that \Neven under Lainie's fascination.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.17,0:16:28.37,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I still hold her in the \Nhighest regard, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.67,0:16:30.76,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,And what of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.85,0:16:38.56,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Royalty should never let their emotions\Nlead them into poor decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.56,0:16:41.00,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,That's been drilled into me all my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.00,0:16:43.59,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,as the one and only heir to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.52,0:16:47.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So you'd just take Lainie's magicite \Nfrom her without a second thought?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.94,0:16:50.33,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Yes. My emotions are secondary.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.64,0:16:54.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And you think becoming a vampire \Nis the right thing for royalty to do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.87,0:16:57.25,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You're the last one \NI want to hear that from.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.91,0:17:00.87,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,What is that on your back, pray tell?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.79,0:17:04.12,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You may not have absorbed \Nthe magicite in the same way,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.12,0:17:07.86,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,but we both sought the powers of monsters—\Na vampire and a dragon—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.86,0:17:09.53,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,just the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.03,0:17:13.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You and I are in very different positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.55,0:17:16.61,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.61,0:17:19.74,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You're a princess who threw away your \Nright to the throne like it was nothing,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.74,0:17:22.77,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,and I'm the one and only crown prince \Nwho was left behind!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.14,0:17:24.85,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Our positions {\i1}are{\i0} different!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.23,0:17:26.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.81,0:17:29.62,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,That's why I had no choice but to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.11,0:17:35.04,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I will use the power of a vampire \Nto seize control of this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.04,0:17:36.74,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Seize control?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.24,0:17:41.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But why?! You'd still be the next king, \Neven if you hadn't done that!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.99,0:17:46.76,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,If you sincerely believe that, \Nyou really have been oblivious.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.48,0:17:52.20,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,How many people have truly \Naccepted me as the next king?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.79,0:17:55.37,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You can't tell me you haven't \Nheard people saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.37,0:18:00.52,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,"If only Princess Anisphia \Nhad a talent for magic"!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.18,0:18:05.33,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Everyone acknowledges you, \Nridicules you, and fears you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.84,0:18:09.29,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You are genuinely a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.29,0:18:10.16,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.63,0:18:13.44,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,No ordinary human can \Nmatch up to a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.44,0:18:15.87,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,So I have no choice but to become one!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.87,0:18:18.11,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,If there's no other way, then so be it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.11,0:18:21.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You're wrong! That's not the kind of king \Npeople want you to be!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.56,0:18:25.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Can't you just treasure the ties \Nthat bind people to each other,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.15,0:18:29.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and be a king who works hand-in-hand \Nwith them to lead the kingdom?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.04,0:18:31.76,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,A king like that can only \Nbe called ornamental!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.22,0:18:36.49,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,The ties that bind people? \NWorking hand-in-hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.00,0:18:39.46,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Well, I... I've seen it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.80,0:18:42.64,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,The rifts that gape between \Ncommoner and commoner!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.66,0:18:46.67,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,The arrogance of nobles who don't \Neven see commoners as people!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.67,0:18:49.67,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,In this kingdom, magic is everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.10,0:18:53.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Which is why you should be \Na king who changes that!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.66,0:18:54.89,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It can't be changed!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.89,0:18:57.12,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,What happened when the previous king
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.12,0:19:00.46,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,extolled commoners \Nand gave them noble titles?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.23,0:19:03.81,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,A revolt!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.81,0:19:05.95,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,One that involved many of the nobles!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.37,0:19:09.46,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Even now, after Father and Duke put it down,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.46,0:19:11.92,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,its flames still smolder!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.63,0:19:16.95,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,This kingdom is ill.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.95,0:19:20.10,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,So I have no choice but to change it \Nwith absolute power.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.10,0:19:23.32,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Power great enough to shatter \Nthe unchangeable norm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.64,0:19:25.51,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.62,0:19:28.19,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I couldn't do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.57,0:19:30.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.33,0:19:34.13,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I'm a foolish commoner \Nwho doesn't even compare to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.58,0:19:37.71,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I couldn't excel in anything. \NI could do nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.71,0:19:39.93,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,No matter how hard I tried,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.93,0:19:43.14,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,all I could do was things that were \Npossible if I just worked at them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.48,0:19:47.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And that's why you sought power, \Neven if you had to steal it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.87,0:19:52.00,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It's power that is necessary \Nto correct this misguided kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.38,0:19:56.70,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,And you have no right to say \Na single thing about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.30,0:19:59.56,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Anisphia Wynn Palettia.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.00,0:20:02.01,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,You are the first princess,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.01,0:20:04.96,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,and you threw away the responsibilities \Nburned into that name.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.78,0:20:08.79,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,This is the future you chose not to pursue.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.79,0:20:12.01,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,If it's something a monster \Ncould throw away so easily,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.01,0:20:15.04,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,what problem is there with a foolish \Ncommoner like me vomiting blood
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.04,0:20:16.77,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,for the chance to pick it up?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.77,0:20:20.03,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Al, tell me one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.03,0:20:22.11,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What is magic to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.11,0:20:24.71,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It's a curse, Sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.66,0:20:30.93,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Magic, the royal blood, \Nmy position as a prince...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.30,0:20:33.41,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,To me, they're all curses.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.94,0:20:37.51,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,They're meant to reduce me to nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.72,0:20:39.82,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.73,0:20:43.13,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Fine, Algard.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.13,0:20:47.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Maybe the place where you stand right now \Nis something I threw away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.32,0:20:50.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But I can't allow that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.20,0:20:54.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you're going to pick up the \Nfuture that I threw away,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.55,0:20:58.45,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,then I'll pick up the present \Nthat {\i1}you{\i0} just threw away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.22,0:21:01.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,A kingdom ruled by an inhumane king
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.81,0:21:03.61,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,who hurts people and \Ntramples them underfoot
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.14,0:21:06.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,is not a kingdom where \Npeople can live happily.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.06,0:21:10.02,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,None are more unfortunate than a people \Nruled by a king who lacks power!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.02,0:21:13.41,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Power? How very comical.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.41,0:21:16.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you really so vain as \Nto believe you can beat me
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.23,0:21:19.21,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,when we fight on equal ground?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.84,0:21:22.42,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,How dare you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.77,0:21:24.87,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If power really is everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.87,0:21:26.94,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,then let's see you beat me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.94,0:21:31.64,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,I told you that you do not have \Nthe right to stand in my way!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.83,0:21:34.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,No. I will stop my brother's little game.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.89,0:21:36.85,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's my right as your older sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.18,0:21:40.05,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,It's too late for that nonsense now!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.72,0:21:44.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yes, it really is... too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.24,0:21:46.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But, you know...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.71,0:21:48.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Magic is made up of prayers for tomorrow
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.90,0:21:52.95,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and wishes for everyone's happiness, Al.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.32,0:21:54.49,Default,Algard,0,0,0,,Sister...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.40,0:21:57.78,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Face me, Algard!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.21,0:22:01.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I reject your definition!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.00,0:22:05.01,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Eight\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Magic Definition of the \NMonster and the Commoner
